    VERIFIER_UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN.
A verifier's inability to execute a proof profile is not proof that the credential is invalid. Unsupported or
verifier-unknown status remains typed non-PASS with reason and re-verification/appeal route where applicable.

Justice / urgent preservation:
    justice is a guarded proceeding-profile transition graph, not an unconditional linear chain;
    urgent preservation must be preauthorized, bounded, expiry/review/release governed and non-self-renewing;
    expiry invalidates retry, failover, delayed continuation, queue replay and continuity use of the old authority;
    action after expiry requires fresh current competent authority and fresh required evaluation;
    uncertain prior external effect preserves PARTIAL_EFFECT / OUTCOME_UNKNOWN and requires reconciliation before unsafe
    replay;
    a mandatory appeal/contestability route cannot be deleted by profile configuration.

52.4 HUMAN-EFFECT / REVIEW STATUS BINDING

Human-Effect Closure is CURRENT as a semantic rule over existing owners. This text edition does not invent a standalone
SchemaID merely because the rule has a name. Where executable owner/schema/profile/test binding remains unresolved, the
machine-binding status is MACHINE_BINDING_INCOMPLETE rather than PASS.

The existence of a reviewed rule, receipt name, test obligation, or documentation clause does not imply executable
certification, empirical validation, production safety or canonical admission.

53. STANDALONE 15.x SEMANTIC CLOSURE

v15.10 is a standalone current source. Its meaning does not depend on an older release being present.

Current-source roles:
    BOOK       explanatory human projection;
    TECHNICAL  controlling abstract structure, rules, algorithms and build/reading contract;
    CATALOGUE  controlling detailed inventory plus the embedded 15.x retention corpus;
    HISTORY    lineage only, non-controlling.

The Catalogue's embedded retention corpus is part of the current v15.10 source, not an external predecessor dependency.
It exists so that compaction cannot silently delete a unique earlier 15.x rule, exception, equation, test meaning,
nonclaim, scope condition, ordering condition or status distinction before that meaning is fully normalized into the new
abstract owners.

Current reading is deterministic:
    1. read the structured current Technical + Catalogue definitions;
    2. read stable current identifiers and explicit status/disposition records;
    3. read the embedded RetentionSeed corpus;
    4. where an explicit current definition names the same stable identifier/family and states a supersession, the
       current structured owner controls that scope;
    5. otherwise the retained seed remains a current compatibility semantic inside this release;
    6. History and external predecessor files never override the current source.

No retained seed gains new authority merely by retention. Retention preserves prior meaning; it cannot widen authority,
convert CANDIDATE/DEFERRED/RESEARCH into CURRENT, turn UNKNOWN into PASS, or convert specification into proof,
implementation, empirical validation or certification.

A future release may remove a RetentionSeed only when it records an exact replacement owner and demonstrates that the
replacement preserves the seed's applicable permissions, obligations, prohibitions, exceptions, nonclaims, scope,
ordering/timing conditions and status. Mere similarity or model confidence is insufficient.

RetentionClosureReceipt/v1 records at minimum:
    candidate source hashes;
    embedded retained-source hashes;
    stable-identity counts and missing-ID list;
    semantic-leaf span verification;
    formula/operator source-line verification;
    current structured-owner collision/reference checks;
    explicit supersession/disposition map;
    unresolved retention debt;
    verifier/tool identity and evidence refs.

Required standalone checks:
    STANDALONE-T01 deleting every external v15.x file does not remove current meaning;
    STANDALONE-T02 every retained stable ID remains discoverable in current Technical/Catalogue or the current retention
                    registry;
    STANDALONE-T03 every semantic-leaf source span validates against the embedded current retention corpus;
    STANDALONE-T04 every retained formula/operator candidate resolves to exact current embedded text;
    STANDALONE-T05 no retained historical status is silently promoted;
    STANDALONE-T06 explicit current supersession cannot widen rights/authority/scope without the applicable change path;
    STANDALONE-T07 History is not needed to interpret current Garden;
    STANDALONE-T08 external predecessor hashes may support audit but are never required for current interpretation.

END OF GARDEN v15.10 — TECHNICAL DESIGN
